From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:31:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 168/180] fix(gastown): a lost fast-forward race re-enters the
 rebase step instead of re-rebasing in place (gcp-xs3eq)

merge_ff_push retried a lost race in place: on a failed ff-merge, or a push
rejected because the target moved, it checked out temp, re-rebased it onto the
new tip and pushed again (up to three attempts, from patches/0013, carried by
0056/0095/0097/0104/0144). The tree it landed was therefore not the tree
run-tests ran on. A temp that carried merges (the #374 skip-rebase arm) was
flattened by that re-rebase, and the landed tip was not the tested temp.
Upstream #374 is explicit that re-materializing replaces the tested tree, so a
lost race has to be a step re-entry.

merge_ff_push is now ONE attempt. A lost race calls the new
merge_ff_push_lost_race notice and returns 6, touching neither temp nor the
bead. The lane already drops temp on exit and the step's `*)` arm drains, so
the next patrol re-selects the still-assigned bead, the rebase step rebuilds
temp and run-tests runs again before any push. Status 6 is re-used (its
meaning is now "lost the race") and status 3, which nothing can return any
more, is retired from the script header, result_summary, the formula status
table and the batch lane header. Statuses 0, 2, 5 and 7 are unchanged, as is
the push-rejection classification: a moved target is a lost race (6), a target
that stood still is a veto (7).

Tests: the in-place-retry cases are replaced by cases that pin the new
contract. test_lost_race_stops_for_a_rebase_reentry and
test_lost_race_leaves_a_merge_topology_temp_unflattened (new) assert status 6,
the racing commit left on origin, temp byte-identical to what the tests saw.
The moving-target, script status 6, lane and batch land cases assert exactly
one push attempt and the drain. The conflicting re-rebase cases (push status 3,
script status 3, batch dropped-commit and re-rebase-conflict) are retired with
the code they covered; the batch suite goes from 22 to 20 cases.

Cost, accepted by the mayor ruling (gcp-bdgg1): one extra patrol and test run
per lost race. patches/ is regenerated with `make patches` in this commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
